  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEDOUTI - Improving the Security Environment and Consolidating Peace through Community-Based Reintegration of Ex-combatants in the Central African Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project proposes to support the reintegration of combatants who will be disarmed and demobilized under the National Program for Disarmament, Demobilization, Reintegration and Rehabilitation, as well as other individuals associated with armed groups or vulnerable to their (re)recruitment but who are not part of the PNDDR. The Project plans to consider 750 ex-combatants who will be identified by the UEPNDDRR for reintegration activities in the communities. The project will also support another 750 community-based beneficiaries identified through consultations with local dialogue and peace mechanisms. In addition to traditional reintegration activities for ex-combatants, the project also offers a psychological support service package that will be part of a trauma healing process to identify potential remobilization factors and prepare ex-combatants for easy reintegration. This first step will pave the way for all other resocialization, empowerment, and social cohesion activities. In this community-based reintegration approach, the eligible ex-combatants will participate in the implementation of project activities along with other members of the communities targeted. In addition, the project will give pride of place to women and youth at risk in its implementation to take advantage of the benefits and opportunities of their greater participation in formal and informal peacebuilding mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
